<title>USA: Medical Tech sees FY97 revs up to $12 mln.</title>
<headline>Medical Tech sees FY97 revs up to $12 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BOCA RATON, Fla. 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medical Technology &amp; Innovations Inc said Thursday it believes FY 97 revenues will grow by more than 1000 percent to between $11.6 and $12.3 million.</p>
<p>In August the company completed its acquisition of Steridyne Corp of Riviera Beach, Florida. Medical Technology said its projections for Steridyne products show a doubling of revenues over the next 12 months.</p>
<p>The company is projecting annual per share earnings to increase from a $0.16 loss in 1996 to a $0.11 profit in 1997.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
